# Build context for every image is the repository root. Safe superset: the
# per-image lists (backend/Dockerfile.dockerignore, frontend/Dockerfile.dockerignore)
# take precedence for their image and repeat the essential rules, so nothing
# here is the only line of defence.
#
# `**/` throughout: a bare name only matches at the context root, so
# `uploads` would not stop backend/uploads, `tests` would not stop
# backend/tests, and a host install or build nested in a workspace member
# would leak into COPY and clobber the clean in-image one.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# Monaco bundle copied by frontend/scripts/copy-monaco.mjs; its version stamp
# must come from the in-image install, not the host.
**/public/monaco
.git
**/.claude
**/.serena
**/.code-review-graph
**/.playwright-mcp
# Operator-owned data and tooling, never part of an image.
**/uploads
**/monitoring
**/plans
**/docs
# dotenv files can hold secrets; only the example is allowed through.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/*.md
# Not needed at runtime: tests and their config.
**/tests
**/jest.config.js
**/email.html
# Dockerfiles and ignore lists are read by the builder itself, not COPY'd.
**/Dockerfile*
**/.dockerignore
